WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.679 --> 00:00:08.530
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
Legend Of Korra did a big hat tip to a very

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:12.870
specific last airbender episode and made a
huge reveal that I think made everyone fall

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:16.010
out of their chairs at new york comic con.

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:19.510
The Korra panel was yesterday and I posted
the whole video so I’ll add a link to that

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:21.140
in the description.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:25.590
I’ll explain all the important stuff Bryke
said after my review.

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.630
Careful for spoilers from the episode if you
haven’t seen it.

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:30.550
I’ll wait just a sec....okay, here we go.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:31.550
Top 5 Moments,

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.719
Number 5 - Korra Alone

00:00:33.719 --> 00:00:37.690
The title of the episode is homage to the
last airbender episode Zuko alone.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:40.010
That was book 2 episode 7.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:43.880
Both of these episode are about not being
able to run away from your identity.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:47.180
In the last airbender episode Zuko decides
that he’s better off on his own, leaves

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:51.489
Iroh and tries to pretend like he’s not
a prince of the fire nation.

00:00:51.489 --> 00:00:56.250
Eventually something happens and he realizes
he can’t run from who he is.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.219
It’s the exact same thing for Korra.

00:00:58.219 --> 00:01:01.579
She can’t run from her identity as the avatar.

00:01:01.579 --> 00:01:04.519
She keeps hallucinating herself in the avatar
state.

00:01:04.519 --> 00:01:07.220
The vision literally chains itself to her.

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:12.030
I did love that they explained the fight scene
we saw at the end of episode 1.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:15.310
She went into the fight feeling like she was
facing herself.

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:19.800
She wasn’t part of some underground MMA
ring.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:23.770
I do wonder if she would have stayed there
had she won the fight.

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:25.310
That’s not really the point of the exercise
though.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:27.299
Her true identity will always win out.

00:01:27.299 --> 00:01:30.470
And for those wondering about Korra reconnecting
with her past lives.

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:32.509
The title of this episode says it all.

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:36.200
Mike and Bryan really wanted Korra to be on
her own.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.799
She can’t turn inward for guidance or quick
answers anymore.

00:01:38.799 --> 00:01:43.659
That doesn’t mean she won’t ever be able
to reconnect with them but at least for now.

00:01:43.659 --> 00:01:46.020
She’s completely on her own.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:48.119
Number 4 - The Flashback

00:01:48.119 --> 00:01:52.189
We finally saw where that teaser clip came
from, right after the book 3 finale.

00:01:52.189 --> 00:01:54.330
And we got an awesome Katara scene.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:58.229
I love that Katara is still such an important
and relevant figure in the Water Tribe.

00:01:58.229 --> 00:02:02.079
She’s still like the best physical and spiritual
doctor ever.

00:02:02.079 --> 00:02:04.970
So of course Korra is going to go to her for
healing.

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:10.110
The big twist right now is that Bryke always
differentiated Korra from Aang in that Korra

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:12.739
was the gung ho Avatar.

00:02:12.739 --> 00:02:19.079
Aang ran from it at first, it took him the
entire last airbender series to come to terms

00:02:19.079 --> 00:02:20.920
with being Avatar.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:25.439
Korra’s first official line was “I’m
the Avatar, you gotta deal with it”.

00:02:25.439 --> 00:02:26.689
She always wanted to be the Avatar.

00:02:26.689 --> 00:02:27.769
Until now.

00:02:27.769 --> 00:02:32.120
Based on Katara’s explanation, it seems
like Korra is suffering PTSD.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:36.709
She can fix the physical trauma to her body,
but she won’t be able to consciously enter

00:02:36.709 --> 00:02:40.459
the avatar state until she fixes her emotional
trauma.

00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:44.710
For those asking, yes, I do think if she were
in another life-threatening situation, her

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:47.500
body would automatically enter the avatar
state.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.340
Like when Zaheer was poisoning her.

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:52.790
Right now, that’s the only way for her to
enter the avatar state.

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:58.439
I’m curious to see how many more episodes
go by before she fixes herself.

00:02:58.439 --> 00:03:00.269
Number 3 - Korra does Star Wars

00:03:00.269 --> 00:03:06.749
Bryke are huge Star Wars fans, so if you got
an empire strikes back vibe from part of the

00:03:06.749 --> 00:03:09.010
episode, it was intentional.

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:13.439
During the New York Comic Con panel, when
they were explaining Kuvira’s army, they

00:03:13.439 --> 00:03:19.080
said part of the designs were based on Stormtroopers
and GI Joe’s from the 1980s cartoon.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:25.040
Mike and Bryan grew up in the 80s, so they,
just like every other person, were influenced

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:27.530
by those.

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:33.049
The Empire Strikes back thing I’m talking
about is Korra marching through the snow to

00:03:33.049 --> 00:03:35.290
the Spirit Portal to look for guidance.

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:39.180
It reminded me of Luke Skywalker on Hoth getting
the vision of Obi-Wan Kenobi telling him to

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:43.510
go to the swamps of Dagobah to learn from
a wise Master of the force.

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:48.000
So eventually Korra follows one of the spirits
to the earth kingdom swamps to find Toph,

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:56.199
but she doesn’t realize it till it hits
her right 

00:03:56.199 --> 00:03:57.199
in the face.

00:03:57.199 --> 00:04:00.229
Number 2 - Korra’s Search For Raava

00:04:00.229 --> 00:04:03.559
The massive road trip she went on was a lot
of fun because we finally got to see the fire

00:04:03.559 --> 00:04:08.639
nation, but she visits all of the different
bending territories.

00:04:08.639 --> 00:04:16.290
She even runs into the fish vendor from last
airbender with the portrait of Aang.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:18.690
I love that Mike and Bryan leave Aang unchanged.

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:23.420
Like Aang still had that silly sense of humor
even after he and Katara started their family.

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:28.030
The Aang flashbacks in book 1 made him seem
kind of serious even though Toph still called

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:35.240
him twinkle toes.

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:39.310
and my number 1 moment, of course - Melon
Lord is back

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:45.780
Everyone let me know when they figured out
the “who” part.

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:49.300
Because of all the empire strikes back stuff
I was thinking about, I kept thinking Toph

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:55.199
might be in the swamp, so when the spirit
said it brought Korra there to find a “who”

00:04:55.199 --> 00:04:58.229
not a “What” I was like, yep.

00:04:58.229 --> 00:04:59.229
Toph.

00:04:59.229 --> 00:05:02.569
The voice actress playing her was Philece
Sampler for anyone wondering who it was.

00:05:02.569 --> 00:05:06.370
It continues the tradition of them using different
voice actors to do older versions of the last

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:07.789
airbender people.

00:05:07.789 --> 00:05:12.000
The real question now is what has toph been
doing in the swamp all this time and what

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:15.050
is she going to do with Korra to help her
re-connect with Raava?

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:20.070
Toph is a funny character, but if you remember,
until she met Aang and Team Avatar.

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:22.300
She lived a very solitary life.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:26.340
She spent most of her time on her own learning
from the Badger Moles and prize fighting.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:28.199
All hail Melon Lord.

00:05:28.199 --> 00:05:29.199
Who else is hoping we get to see her do some
epic bending.

00:05:29.199 --> 00:05:30.199
Theoretically if the star wars influence holds
strong, Toph would be just as powerful in

00:05:30.199 --> 00:05:31.199
her old age as Yoda was in his.

00:05:31.199 --> 00:05:32.400
So maybe we’ll get to see her smash a bunch
some of the metal bender’s mechs.

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:34.530
This is really a story about Korra, so all
of the attention will be on her and the younger

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:35.530
characters.

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:43.130
But I really hope we get some epic bending
from the old team avatar.

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:48.569
Let me know what your favorite moment was
and how do you think that Toph is going to

00:05:48.569 --> 00:05:49.569
help Korra?

00:05:49.569 --> 00:05:52.660
Overall I gave the episode an A for being
able to go in a vastly different direction

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:57.340
in the current narrative and tell this side
story with just Korra and pay homage to so

00:05:57.340 --> 00:05:59.490
many big last airbender things.

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:02.710
Mike and Bryan are really good about trying
new things with the Korra characters but they

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:06.590
are always happy to do a little fanservice
to their own beloved characters whenever appropriate.

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:11.009
They have said during interviews that they
love bringing last airbender characters back,

00:06:11.009 --> 00:06:15.599
but because episodes are only about 22 minutes
each, they just don’t have time for everything.

00:06:15.599 --> 00:06:19.389
If Korra were an hour long show, or if they
got like double the number of episodes, then

00:06:19.389 --> 00:06:22.699
you’d probably see a lot more episodes like
this, where it follows a single character

00:06:22.699 --> 00:06:24.960
for an extended period of time.

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:31.171
So I will be doing a Q&amp;A for this tomorrow,
be sure to subscribe to get it and

00:06:31.171 --> 00:06:34.580
Just to explain what they said during the
New York Comic Con panel,

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:37.300
Kuvira is the confirmed big villain of the
season.

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:40.530
They spent a lot of time talking about their
concept of the character and the inspiration

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:44.780
for the new metal bending army.

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:52.842
It’s all in the Comic Con video I posted.

00:06:52.842 --> 00:06:57.260
You can click here to see it all and click
here for my Episode 1 video.

00:06:57.260 --> 00:07:02.779
Thanks for watching, now let’s all high
five and rewatch the episode.

